456	+# REVIEW_FIXES_02 — second independent-review pass on `release/v1.3.0`
457	+
458	+## Scope
459	+
460	+One PR on `v1/review-fixes-02`, branched from `origin/release/v1.3.0` at `79ebb92c`. It addresses
461	+the findings of the independent review of `028a0826..a22aa1cb` that were still open at the release
462	+head. PR #735 (`c72cf053`, the `test-matrix (24)` timeout fix) had already closed F2 before this
463	+slice started, so F2 is not changed here. No merge, tag or publish is part of this slice: the owner
464	+controls all three.
465	+
466	+## Changes
467	+
468	+| Finding | Fix |
469	+| ------- | --- |
470	+| F1 — turn flow can report VERIFIED after a self-weakening test (HIGH) | `spine_handlers.ts` hashes all workspace test files immediately before and after the verifier. A difference — including a test that rewrites itself back to its base content before exit, or an unreadable/oversized snapshot — makes the pass unbound: `isDeliverableBound` is false, the independence detail names the mutation, and the outcome ladder can reach at most REGRESSION_FREE. A regression reproduces PR #707's self-restoring test through `agent.runTurn()`. |
471	+| F3 — GV-3 replay hid chain integrity | `nexus flights replay` prints `FlightPlayer.describeIntegrity(integrity)` from `loadFlight`. A CLI test edits a flight record and asserts the tamper is named at position 4 of 6. |
472	+| F4 — VR-1's independent reviewer was absent | `nexus verify` now runs a deterministic reviewer over the recorded evidence package (no implementer narrative, no model or credentials needed for the CI gate). It emits the project's structured `ACCEPT`/`REJECT` verdict with verified observations, suspected defects, unproven criteria and scope violations, prints it in the text output, and withholds VERIFIED through the new `REVIEW_REJECTED` reason (BLOCKED, exit 3) when receipts contradict the claim. It never raises a lower verdict. The result schema moves from v2 to v3 because `review` changes meaning. |
473	+| F5 — cancelled scheduler units returned to RUNNABLE | `ConvergenceScheduler.apply("cancelled")` now blocks with cause `EXECUTION_UNKNOWN` and an explicit `replay the step` decision; an eligible alternate is no longer tried automatically. A scheduler test asserts one submission, a BLOCKED unit and the decision. |
